.TH HOWDY.INI 5 "@HOWDY_MAN_DATE@" "Howdy Next @PROJECT_VERSION@" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
howdy.ini \- Howdy Next configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I @HOWDY_CONFIG_PATH_ROFF@
configures Howdy Next using standard INI sections and
.B key = value
lines:
.PP
.nf
[section]
key = value
.fi
.PP
Lines starting with
.B #
or
.B ;
are comments.
Omitted keys use their defaults;
.B howdy set
and
.B howdy disable
only update keys already in the file.
A blank file or one containing a NUL byte is rejected as damaged (keep at least
one comment to use all defaults); run
.B howdy config
to repair it.
.SH "CONFIGURATION OPTIONS"
@HOWDY_CONFIG_REFERENCE@
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @HOWDY_CONFIG_PATH_ROFF@
Configuration file.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR howdy (1),
.BR pam_howdy (8)
